# Commit message template for Insight Replay.
# Conventional Commits 1.0.0 — https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
#
# Format:
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
#   <body>
#
#   <footer>
#
# Edit the lines below the `# ---` cut. Everything above is documentation.
# Lines starting with `#` are stripped by git before the message is saved.
#
# Types (lowercase, pick exactly one):
#   feat     A new feature (user-facing).
#   fix      A bug fix (user-facing).
#   perf     A code change that improves performance.
#   refactor A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature.
#   style    Formatting, whitespace, semicolons — no production code change.
#   test     Adding or correcting tests.
#   docs     Documentation only changes.
#   chore    Build, deps, config, tooling — no production code change.
#   ci       Changes to CI pipelines / workflows.
#   security Hardening that closes a security gap (use when fix(security) is too vague).
#
# Scopes (optional but encouraged — pick the area most affected):
#   api             API route handlers under src/app/api/**.
#   ui              React components under src/components/**.
#   db              Prisma schema, migrations, db lib.
#   track           Tracking SDK + ingest (/api/track/**, src/lib/track.ts).
#   live            Socket.io live service (mini-services/live-service).
#   ai              LLM-powered routes + helpers (src/lib/ai*, /api/**/ai/**).
#   security        Auth, rate-limit, CORS, sanitization, audit, headers.
#   observability   Logs, metrics, health, request IDs, middleware.
#   test            Test files under tests/**.
#   docs            Markdown under docs/**, AGENTS.md, README.
#   ci              .github/workflows/**, scripts/check-quality.sh.
#
# Subject rules:
#   - Imperative mood: "add", "fix", "refactor" — not "added" / "fixes".
#   - Lowercase first letter, no trailing period.
#   - <= 72 characters.
#   - What changed, not why (the why goes in the body).
#
# Body rules:
#   - Wrap at 72 columns.
#   - Explain WHAT and WHY (not HOW — the diff already shows how).
#   - One blank line between subject and body, and between body and footer.
#   - Bullet points with `-` are fine; keep them tight.
#
# Footer rules:
#   - BREAKING CHANGE: <description> on its own line → bumps MAJOR.
#   - `!` after the type/scope also signals a breaking change
#     (e.g. `feat(api)!: drop v1 response envelope`).
#   - Reference issues / PRs / ADRs:
#       Closes #123
#       Refs #456
#       See docs/adr/0007-*.md
#   - Co-authored-by trailers go at the very bottom.
#
# --- cut here ---

# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body — what + why, wrapped at 72 cols>
#
# <footer — BREAKING CHANGE: / Closes # / Refs # / See docs/adr/>

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 1 — feature
# feat(ui): add retention cohort matrix on Retention tab
#
# Surfaces week-over-week retention so PMs can spot cohort decay without
# exporting to a spreadsheet. Reuses the existing /api/projects/[id]/retention
# endpoint; cohort cells are keyboard-navigable (aria-label per cell).
#
# Closes #142
# See docs/adr/0005-in-memory-cache-for-stats.md
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 2 — fix with breaking flag
# fix(api)!: return 404 (not 200 + {error}) when project is missing
#
# The previous 200+error envelope hid missing-project cases from clients that
# only checked status codes, causing silent UI fallbacks. Standardized on the
# api-response.ts envelope; clients must now branch on status, not body.error.
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: /api/projects/[id]/* now returns 404 for unknown ids
# Refs #98
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example 3 — chore
# chore(ci): cache bun install in ci.yml on bun.lock hash
#
# Cuts ~40s off cold CI runs by reusing the bun install cache across runs.
# Falls back to a partial-key restore so a bumped dep still hits the cache.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
